{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the angel of YHWH found her.</b> He found her prepared for divine visions, and accordingly He appeared to her." "<b>By the spring of water.</b> She was praying, as he explains by saying: כִּי שָׁמַע ה' אֶל עָנְיֵךְ (Genesis 16:11)." "<b>On the way (עַל הָעַיִן).</b> At the mother of the road; and when there are two roads they are called עֵינַיִם (eyes), and the place where the two roads begin is called פֶּתַח עֵינַיִם (opening of eyes), which is what our Rabbis of blessed memory called פָּרָשַׁת דְּרָכִים (a fork of roads) (Ketubot 17a)." "<b>On the way to Shur.</b> This is Hagra, as Onkelos translates it, and it is a city on the border of the land of Israel or outside it, as our Rabbis of blessed memory stated in Gittin (2a). He thereby indicates that she intended at that time to leave the land of Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:20.558649216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}